PocketAgent (Phase 0) - third-party software and licenses
==========================================================

This repository contains only build scripts and app source. The binaries that end up in a built
APK are fetched, checksummed and compiled by CI; none of them is committed here.

proot  (GPL-2.0-or-later)
  Bundled as lib/arm64-v8a/libproot.so and libproot-loader.so, built from source by
  proot/build-proot.sh.
  Source:  https://github.com/termux/proot   (pinned commit in proot/build-proot.sh, tag v5.1.107.102)
  Upstream: https://github.com/proot-me/proot
  proot runs as a separate executable; the app and the rootfs only invoke it. The complete
  corresponding source is available at the URL above (the exact commit is recorded in the
  "proot-build.info" file attached to every release and in the APK's assets/proot.info).

talloc  (LGPL-3.0-or-later)
  Statically linked into libproot.so.
  Source:  https://download.samba.org/pub/talloc/talloc-2.4.3.tar.gz   (SHA-256 pinned in proot/build-proot.sh)
  To relink proot against a modified talloc, run proot/build-proot.sh with a patched tarball.

Debian GNU/Linux 13 "trixie" userland  (various free-software licenses)
  The rootfs is a minimal Debian system created with debootstrap (arm64). Every package's license is
  in /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright inside the rootfs (kept deliberately); package sources are
  available from https://deb.debian.org/debian and https://snapshot.debian.org.

Hermes Agent  (MIT)
  https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent, release v0.23.3, installed unmodified by
  rootfs/install-hermes.sh using the project's own installer stages. Its Python dependencies keep
  their own licenses (see the packages' metadata inside the rootfs).

Python (PSF License) and uv (MIT/Apache-2.0)
  Provisioned by the Hermes installer inside the rootfs.

Android app dependencies
  AndroidX, Jetpack Compose, Material 3, Kotlin standard library and kotlinx.coroutines  (Apache-2.0)
  Apache Commons Compress  (Apache-2.0)
  XZ for Java  (public domain / 0BSD)

GPL/LGPL source offer
  For any of the GPL/LGPL components above, the build scripts in this repository plus the pinned
  upstream sources reproduce the shipped binaries. If a link above stops working, open an issue
  in this repository and the sources will be provided.
